From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: scp: bound the complete DRAM recovery mapping

In Nothing OS 4.1 device modules ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12,
scp_recovery_init() maps ROUNDUP(ap_dram_size, 1024) * 4 whenever the
signed DRAM size is positive, independently of scp_dram_region. Checking
only the unrounded single region when that DT flag is set leaves both
an unchecked mapping path and arithmetic/address wrap in the backup span.

Validate every advertised DRAM range, including the four rounded banks,
before recovery setup. Use checked u32 arithmetic to match the existing
consumer and reject sizes that could also change its signed predicate.
An absent DRAM range remains allowed only when DT does not require it.

This is structural validation, not proof of carveout ownership or firmware
authentication. Keep SCP/DVFS disabled. Apply after 0093; this candidate is
deliberately not wired into APKBUILD pending integration review.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
@@ -2158,6 +2158,21 @@ static bool scp_region_range_valid(u32 start, u32 size)
 	return start && size && !check_add_overflow(start, size, &end);
 }
 
+static bool scp_region_dram_valid(u32 start, u32 size)
+{
+	u32 rounded, span;
+
+	if (!size || check_add_overflow(size, 1023U, &rounded))
+		return false;
+	rounded &= ~1023U;
+
+	/* Recovery maps four 1 KiB-aligned banks, including backups. */
+	if (check_mul_overflow(rounded, 4U, &span))
+		return false;
+
+	return scp_region_range_valid(start, span);
+}
+
 static int scp_region_info_validate(void)
 {
 	if (scp_region_info_copy.struct_size < sizeof(scp_region_info_copy)) {
@@ -2183,10 +2198,12 @@ static int scp_region_info_validate(void)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (scpreg.scp_dram_region == 1 &&
-	    !scp_region_range_valid(scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_start,
-				    scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_size)) {
-		pr_err("[SCP] invalid DRAM region-info\n");
+	if ((scpreg.scp_dram_region == 1 ||
+	     scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_start ||
+	     scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_size) &&
+	    !scp_region_dram_valid(scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_start,
+				   scp_region_info_copy.ap_dram_size)) {
+		pr_err("[SCP] invalid DRAM recovery span in region-info\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
